E('titanic|rms titanic|sinking of the titanic', 'The RMS Titanic was a British passenger liner that sank on her maiden voyage.', 'She hit an iceberg late on 14 April 1912 and sank early on 15 April.',
  'She was sailing from Southampton to New York.', 'She was the largest ship afloat at the time and was called “practically unsinkable”.', 'There were lifeboats for only about half the people aboard.', 'More than 1,500 people died.', 'The wreck was found in 1985, about 3,800 metres down.',
  'Her loss led to new safety rules, including lifeboats for everyone.')
E('chernobyl|chernobyl disaster', 'The Chernobyl disaster was the worst nuclear power accident in history.', 'It happened on 26 April 1986, in Soviet Ukraine.',
  'A reactor exploded during a safety test.', 'Radioactive material spread across Europe.', 'The nearby town of Pripyat was evacuated and remains abandoned.', 'Thirty-one people died in the immediate aftermath, and many more later from radiation.', 'A large exclusion zone still surrounds the site.',
  'It changed attitudes to nuclear safety worldwide.')
E('9/11|september 11|september 11 attacks|twin towers|world trade center', 'The September 11 attacks were terrorist attacks on the United States by al-Qaeda.', 'They happened on 11 September 2001.',
  'Nineteen hijackers took over four passenger planes.', 'Two hit the Twin Towers of the World Trade Center in New York, which collapsed.', 'One hit the Pentagon near Washington.', 'Passengers fought back on the fourth plane, which crashed in Pennsylvania.', 'Nearly 3,000 people were killed.', 'The US launched a war in Afghanistan soon after.',
  'They reshaped security, travel and world politics.')
E('moon landing hoax', 'The Moon landings were real.', 'Six Apollo missions landed between 1969 and 1972.',
  'Astronauts brought back 382 kilograms of Moon rock.', 'Mirrors left on the Moon are still used to bounce lasers from Earth.', 'Independent countries, including the USSR, tracked the missions.',
  'Spacecraft orbiting the Moon have photographed the landing sites.')
E('covid|covid-19|coronavirus|pandemic|covid 19', 'COVID-19 is a disease caused by the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus that caused a global pandemic.', 'It was first identified in late 2019, and the WHO declared a pandemic in March 2020.',
  'Countries introduced lockdowns, masks and social distancing.', 'Vaccines were developed in under a year.', 'Millions of people died worldwide.', 'The WHO ended the global health emergency in May 2023.',
  'It changed how people work, travel and think about public health.')
E('spanish flu|1918 flu|1918 pandemic', 'The 1918 influenza pandemic, often called the Spanish flu, was one of the deadliest in history.', 'It spread from 1918 to 1920.',
  'It infected about a third of the world’s population.', 'It killed an estimated 50 million people.', 'Unusually, it killed many healthy young adults.', 'It was called “Spanish” because neutral Spain reported on it freely.',
  'It shaped modern public health.')
E('great fire of london', 'The Great Fire of London destroyed much of the medieval city.', 'It burned from 2 to 6 September 1666.',
  'It began in a bakery on Pudding Lane.', 'It destroyed over 13,000 houses and St Paul’s Cathedral.', 'Surprisingly few deaths were recorded.', 'Christopher Wren rebuilt St Paul’s and many churches.',
  'It led to new building rules using brick and stone.')
E('fall of the soviet union|collapse of the soviet union|soviet union|ussr', 'The Soviet Union was a communist state that existed from 1922 to 1991.', 'It dissolved on 26 December 1991.',
  'It was made up of 15 republics, with Russia the largest.', 'It was a superpower rival to the United States in the Cold War.', 'Its economy stagnated in the 1970s and 1980s.', 'Gorbachev’s reforms loosened control.', 'Its republics declared independence one after another in 1991.',
  'Its collapse ended the Cold War.')
E('european union|eu', 'The European Union is a political and economic union of European countries.', 'It grew from the European Coal and Steel Community of 1951 and became the EU in 1993.',
  'It has 27 member states.', 'Many members share the euro currency, introduced in 2002.', 'People and goods can move freely between most members.', 'The UK left in 2020.', 'It won the Nobel Peace Prize in 2012.',
  'It was created to make war between European nations unthinkable.')
E('brexit', 'Brexit was the United Kingdom’s departure from the European Union.', 'The referendum was held on 23 June 2016, and the UK left on 31 January 2020.',
  'About 52 per cent voted to leave.', 'Negotiations took years.', 'The UK and EU agreed a trade deal in December 2020.',
  'It remains one of the most debated decisions in modern British politics.')
E('arab spring', 'The Arab Spring was a wave of protests and uprisings across the Arab world.', 'It began in Tunisia in December 2010 and spread in 2011.',
  'It started after a street vendor, Mohamed Bouazizi, set himself on fire in protest.', 'Leaders fell in Tunisia, Egypt, Libya and Yemen.', 'Syria descended into a long civil war.',
  'Its outcomes ranged from democracy in Tunisia to war and repression elsewhere.')
E('2008 financial crisis|financial crisis|great recession', 'The 2008 financial crisis was the worst global economic crisis since the Great Depression.', 'It peaked in 2008.',
  'It began with risky mortgage lending in the United States.', 'The investment bank Lehman Brothers collapsed in September 2008.', 'Governments bailed out banks.', 'Unemployment rose sharply worldwide.',
  'It led to tighter banking rules.')
E('chinese civil war', 'The Chinese Civil War was fought between the Nationalists and the Communists.', 'It was fought mainly from 1927 to 1949.',
  'The Nationalists were led by Chiang Kai-shek.', 'The Communists were led by Mao Zedong.', 'It paused when both fought Japan.', 'The Communists won, and the Nationalists retreated to Taiwan.',
  'It created the People’s Republic of China.')
E('spanish civil war|franco|francisco franco', 'The Spanish Civil War was fought between Republicans and Nationalists.', 'It lasted from 1936 to 1939.',
  'The Nationalists were led by General Francisco Franco.', 'Nazi Germany and Fascist Italy supported Franco.', 'International volunteers fought for the Republic.', 'The bombing of Guernica became a symbol of its horror.', 'Franco ruled Spain as a dictator until his death in 1975.',
  'It was a rehearsal for the Second World War.')
E('rwandan genocide|rwanda', 'The Rwandan genocide was the mass murder of Tutsi people in Rwanda.', 'It happened over about 100 days from April to July 1994.',
  'Around 800,000 people, mostly Tutsi, were killed.', 'Many killers were ordinary neighbours, urged on by radio propaganda.', 'The world largely failed to intervene.', 'The Rwandan Patriotic Front ended it.',
  'It is remembered as a terrible failure of the world to act.')
E('gulf war', 'The Gulf War was fought by a US-led coalition against Iraq after it invaded Kuwait.', 'Iraq invaded in August 1990; the war ran from January to February 1991.',
  'Saddam Hussein’s forces occupied Kuwait.', 'A coalition of 35 countries was formed.', 'The ground war lasted about 100 hours.',
  'It was the first war widely broadcast live on TV.')
E('iraq war', 'The Iraq War began with a US-led invasion of Iraq.', 'It began in March 2003, and US forces withdrew in 2011.',
  'The invasion overthrew Saddam Hussein.', 'Claims that Iraq had weapons of mass destruction proved false.', 'A long insurgency followed.', 'Hundreds of thousands of people died.',
  'It remains highly controversial.')
E('afghanistan war|war in afghanistan', 'The war in Afghanistan followed the September 11 attacks.', 'It lasted from 2001 to 2021.',
  'A US-led coalition toppled the Taliban government.', 'Osama bin Laden was killed in Pakistan in 2011.', 'The Taliban returned to power when US forces withdrew in August 2021.',
  'It was America’s longest war.')
E('french and indian war|seven years war|seven years’ war', 'The Seven Years’ War was a global conflict between Britain and France and their allies.', 'It lasted from 1756 to 1763.',
  'In North America it was called the French and Indian War.', 'Britain won Canada from France.', 'It left Britain with large debts.',
  'Britain’s efforts to tax the colonies to pay for it helped spark the American Revolution.')
E('opium wars', 'The Opium Wars were two wars between China and Western powers, mainly Britain.', 'They were fought from 1839 to 1842 and 1856 to 1860.',
  'Britain was selling opium to China against Chinese law.', 'China lost both wars.', 'Hong Kong was ceded to Britain.', 'China was forced to open ports to foreign trade.',
  'China remembers this as the start of its “century of humiliation”.')
E('hong kong', 'Hong Kong is a city on China’s southern coast.', 'It was a British colony from 1842 until 1997.',
  'It returned to China under “one country, two systems”.', 'It is a major financial centre.', 'It has one of the world’s most famous skylines.',
  'Its status and freedoms remain a major political issue.')
E('suez canal', 'The Suez Canal is a waterway in Egypt linking the Mediterranean and the Red Sea.', 'It opened in 1869.',
  'It lets ships avoid sailing around Africa.', 'It was built by a French company led by Ferdinand de Lesseps.', 'Egypt nationalised it in 1956, triggering the Suez Crisis.', 'In 2021 the ship Ever Given blocked it for six days.',
  'It is one of the world’s most important trade routes.')
E('panama canal', 'The Panama Canal is a waterway connecting the Atlantic and Pacific oceans.', 'It opened in 1914.',
  'France first tried to build it in the 1880s and failed.', 'The US completed it.', 'Thousands of workers died, many from disease.', 'Locks lift ships about 26 metres.', 'Panama took full control in 1999.',
  'It transformed global shipping.')
E('gold rush|california gold rush', 'The California Gold Rush was a mass migration after gold was found in California.', 'It began in 1848.',
  'Around 300,000 people rushed there.', 'They were called “forty-niners”.', 'San Francisco grew from a small town to a city.', 'Native Americans suffered terribly.',
  'It sped California to statehood in 1850.')
E('wild west|american frontier|cowboys', 'The Wild West refers to the American frontier in the late 19th century.', 'It is usually associated with roughly 1865 to 1895.',
  'Settlers, ranchers and miners pushed west.', 'Cowboys drove cattle to railways.', 'Native American nations were forced onto reservations.', 'Famous figures include Wild Bill Hickok, Calamity Jane and Billy the Kid.',
  'It became a lasting myth in films and books.')
E('salem witch trials', 'The Salem witch trials were a series of witchcraft prosecutions in colonial Massachusetts.', 'They took place in 1692 and 1693.',
  'Over 200 people were accused.', 'Nineteen were hanged, and one man was pressed to death with stones.', 'Several accusers were young girls.', 'Massachusetts later apologised.',
  'They became a lesson about hysteria and injustice.')
E('boston tea party', 'The Boston Tea Party was a protest against British taxation.', 'It took place on 16 December 1773.',
  'Colonists dumped 342 chests of tea into Boston Harbor.', 'They protested the Tea Act and “taxation without representation”.', 'Britain responded with harsh laws.',
  'It helped lead to the American Revolution.')
